---
description: General Agent Rules
glob: "*"
alwaysApply: true
---

## Agent Behavior (CRITICAL)
- Read readme, docs, skills, rules before planning and coding
- Planning: Follow architecture, strategies, and decisions in `@apps/docu/`
- Execution: Follow architecture, strategies, and decisions in `@apps/docu/`; after implementation (new features and fixes), update docs, readme, and cursor rules if required to keep them aligned
- When creating plans add a ## References section listing cursor rules files and cursor skills you are using
- Summarize assumptions in 3–5 bullets
- Respect Ask mode restrictions (read-only)
- Verify before destructive operations
- Defer to user for ambiguous, high-risk decisions
- Never ask before modifying files (including dotfiles)
- Provide concise summaries when finishing
- Search first (Grep/Glob), read later
- Targeted reads over broad exploration
- Use references strategically
- Maximize parallel calls (batch file reads/searches)

## Code Quality
- Collocate related functionality
- ALWAYS follow linting rules: eslint, biome 
- Search for existing functionality before creating new
- Always use existing packages in codebase before writing custom code
- Never use console, use `@repo/utils/logger/server` or `@repo/utils/logger/client`
- Use `@repo/error` for error handling
- Use `t3-oss` packages for environment variable validation
- Use `lodash-es` (per-function imports)


